<title>THAILAND: Thai Dec CPI up 4.8 pct yr/yr,down 0.1 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Thai Dec CPI up 4.8 pct yr/yr,down 0.1 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's consumer price index (CPI) rose 4.8 percent year-on-year in December, against November's 4.8 percent rise, the Commerce Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The ministry said the 1990-based index rose to 136.3 in December from its 130.1 level in the same month a year ago.</p>
<p>The December CPI eased 0.1 percent from November when it stood at 136.4, against a 0.5 percent month-on-month rise in November over October, the ministry said.  </p>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry issued the following economic indicators:</p>
<p>     THAI CONSUMER PRICES	  Dec 96	Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p>     Month/month			-0.1	  +0.5	 +0.0</p>
<p>     Year/year			  +4.8	  +4.8	 +2.9</p>
<p>     CPI Index (base 1990)	 136.3	 136.4	130.1</p>
<p>     Food/beverage Index	   147.3	 147.6	137.8</p>
<p>     Month/month			-0.2	  +0.0	 -0.1</p>
<p>     Year/year			  +6.9	  +7.0	 +8.1</p>
<p>     Non food/beverage Index     129.0	 128.9	125.1</p>
<p>     Month/month			+0.1	  +0.9	 +0.2</p>
<p>     Year/year			  +3.1	  +3.3	 +4.2</p>
</text>
